{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .head-developer/MEGAPLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Megaplan\n> Generated by the Megaplan skill. Approval is required before the local Codex CLI implementation session starts.\n## Approval Gate\n- Status: Pending user approval\n- To start: reply `approve` in the Codex chat\n- To revise: describe the change before approving\n## Repository\n- Repo: MeharPro/codexa-direct-smoke-01-quote-board-1780177912\n- Repo URL: [https://github.com/MeharPro/codexa-direct-smoke-01-quote-board-1780177912](https://github.com/MeharPro/codexa-direct-smoke-01-quote-board-1780177912)\n- Branch: main\n- Local path: `/Users/meharkhanna/Documents/codexa-workspace/generated-projects/codexa-direct-smoke-01-quote-board-1780177912`\n## User Request\nCreate a new Codexa project named codexa-direct-smoke-01-quote-board-1780177912 and plan a tiny static quote board app with saved favorite quotes. After I approve, build it as a browser-only static app with index.html, styles.css, script.js, a README, local validation, and concise continuous progress updates.\n## Requirement Summary\nCreate a new static Codexa quote board app named `codexa-direct-smoke-01-quote-board-1780177912` using `index.html`, `styles.css`, `script.js`, and `README.md`. It should run in the browser only and save favorite quotes locally. Include local validation and concise progress updates after approval.\n## Technical Requirements\n- Architecture/product scope: A compact static quote board with a quote grid/list, favorite toggles, a favorites view/filter, clear empty states, responsive layout, and localStorage persistence. The implementation will use plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript only.\n- Assumption: Favorites are persisted with browser localStorage.\n- Assumption: The app is static and browser-only with no backend, database, auth, deployment, payments, or external APIs.\n- Assumption: The current project directory is the intended project root.\n- Assumption: Continuous improvement notes should be recorded in `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` without implementing scope-changing ideas unless approved.\n- Local validation expected: test -f index.html; test -f styles.css; test -f script.js; test -f README.md; node --check script.js; test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md\n## Proposed Product Direction\nA compact static quote board with a quote grid/list, favorite toggles, a favorites view/filter, clear empty states, responsive layout, and localStorage persistence. The implementation will use plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript only.\n## Codex Orchestration\n- One local Codex CLI session owns the repo.\n- Codex decides how many internal subagents are useful; for non-trivial work it should prefer visible named responsibility lanes when that is truthful.\n- Subagents are logical Codex responsibilities, not Docker, VM, GKE, or cloud workers.\n- The user can revise subagent use before approval; approval permits Codex to choose the actual internal count and names.\n- If Codex later determines a materially different subagent strategy is needed, it must stop and ask before changing scope, cost, risk, or timeline.\n- The browser flowchart updates rapidly from a parallel Codex flowchart process and shows only the subagents Codex actually reports.\n## Subagent Check-In\n- Advisor recommendation: single-lane Codex run is acceptable.\n- Reason: The Codex planner produced a narrow responsibility split, so a direct implementation lane looks sufficient.\n- User check-in: The plan looks narrow enough for a direct Codex lane. Approval keeps Codex free to ask before changing to a materially different subagent strategy.\n- Likely responsibility areas: Build static app\n- Advisor source: planner_context\n## Continuous Improvement Loop\n- Codex should look for bugs, UX gaps, performance issues, maintainability problems, missing tests, and feature opportunities while implementing.\n- Codex may implement improvements that fit the approved plan or are required for correctness, validation, safety, or a trustworthy MVP.\n- Codex must record deferred ideas in `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` instead of silently expanding scope.\n- Improvements that materially change scope, architecture, data, cost, risk, or timeline require user approval before implementation.\n## Codex Runtime\n- Model: gpt-5.5\n- Coding reasoning: low\n- Planning/model helper reasoning: gpt-5.5 / low\n- Access: full local access\n- Shell environment: inherited from the local supervisor process\n- Account/config/plugins: same local Codex account and CODEX_HOME configuration used by this machine\n## Proposed Internal Responsibilities\n1. Build static app - Create a new static Codexa quote board app named `codexa-direct-smoke-01-quote-board-1780177912` using `index.html`, `styles.css`, `script.js`, and `README.md`. It should run in the browser only and save favorite quotes locally. Include local validation and concise progress updates after approval.. Validation: test -f index.html, test -f styles.css, test -f script.js, test -f README.md, node --check script.js, test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md.\n## Assumptions\n- Favorites are persisted with browser localStorage.\n- The app is static and browser-only with no backend, database, auth, deployment, payments, or external APIs.\n- The current project directory is the intended project root.\n- Continuous improvement notes should be recorded in `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` without implementing scope-changing ideas unless approved.\n## Open Questions\n- None recorded yet.\n## Validation Plan\n- test -f index.html\n- test -f styles.css\n- test -f script.js\n- test -f README.md\n- node --check script.js\n- test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md\n## Completion Bar\n- Files exist in this repo.\n- Validation commands pass or failures are reported honestly.\n- The final summary is grounded in changed files and commands.\n- No docs-only success.\nGenerated: 2026-05-30T21:53:49.168Z\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
